{"timestamp_utc": "2026-02-06T21:38:01.786826+00:00", "user_text": "What is AIT’s mission and vision?", "assistant_text": "The Asian Institute of Technology (AIT) has a clear mission and vision that guide its goals and operations. 

**Vision**: AIT's vision is to transform itself into a respected international graduate institution whose research and education contribute to the development of Asia. This transformation involves making AIT more global, more innovative, more entrepreneurial, and more economically relevant, while leveraging its core strengths in social impact.

**Mission**: AIT's mission is to develop highly qualified and committed professionals who will play a leading role in the sustainable development of the region and its integration into the global economy. This mission is carried out through a focus on education, research, and professional development, with an emphasis on addressing regional and global challenges.", "metrics": {"generation": {"model": "qwen3:8b", "created_at": "2026-02-06T21:38:01.73609526Z", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration_ns": 3366188162, "load_duration_ns": 81371377, "prompt_eval_count": 1405, "prompt_eval_duration_ns": 371492574, "eval_count": 143, "eval_duration_ns": 2863877127, "wall_time_s": 3.3948434259509668, "requested_think": false, "observed_has_thinking_field": false, "tokens_per_second_out": 49.932309822871815}, "retrieval": {"retrieval_wall_time_s": 1.799688415019773, "top_k": 5, "n_returned": 5, "collection_name": "test_v1", "query_len_chars": 33, "has_scores": true, "retrieved_chunk_ids_ranked": ["https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0005", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0005", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0006", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0006", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0000"], "retrieved_source_urls_ranked": ["https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/"]}}, "retrieval_chunks": [{"rank": 1, "chunk_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0005", "score": 0.21495801600084574, "text": "2024 International Green Gown Award in the ‘2030 Climate Action’ category for its transformative project, “Net Zero Campus Initiative: A Leap Towards Sustainable Climate Action.” Supported by the UN Environment Programme and Allianz Global Investors, the award celebrates exemplary sustainability efforts in higher education worldwide. Read more at this link . Vision and Mission Vision Transforming AIT to be a respectable international graduate institution whose research and education contribute to the development of Asia, by making AIT more global, more innovative, more entrepreneurial, and more economically relevant–while leveraging on its social impact core strengths. Mission The mission of AIT in the context of the emerging environment is “to develop highly qualified and committed professionals who will play a leading role in the sustainable development of the region and its integration into the global economy”", "metadata": {"source": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "doc_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about", "chunk_index": 5, "chunk_len_chars": 926, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 2, "chunk_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0005", "score": 0.21495801600084574, "text": "2024 International Green Gown Award in the ‘2030 Climate Action’ category for its transformative project, “Net Zero Campus Initiative: A Leap Towards Sustainable Climate Action.” Supported by the UN Environment Programme and Allianz Global Investors, the award celebrates exemplary sustainability efforts in higher education worldwide. Read more at this link . Vision and Mission Vision Transforming AIT to be a respectable international graduate institution whose research and education contribute to the development of Asia, by making AIT more global, more innovative, more entrepreneurial, and more economically relevant–while leveraging on its social impact core strengths. Mission The mission of AIT in the context of the emerging environment is “to develop highly qualified and committed professionals who will play a leading role in the sustainable development of the region and its integration into the global economy”", "metadata": {"source": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "doc_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about", "chunk_index": 5, "chunk_len_chars": 926, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:23:14.120093+00:00"}}, {"rank": 3, "chunk_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0006", "score": 0.24426153507416182, "text": "Guided by the above clear, timeless vision and mission, the dedicated students, faculty and staff of AIT are set to steer the Institute along its path of becoming: A trailblazer in advanced education in the region, with leadership in IT and new types of multidisciplinary programs An exemplary institution, with an emphasis on academic quality in terms of courses and other aspects of operation A leader in professional development programs A hub for the implementation of regional and transnational research projects, and a research facility for academic professionals", "metadata": {"source": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "doc_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about", "chunk_index": 6, "chunk_len_chars": 569, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 4, "chunk_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0006", "score": 0.24426153507416182, "text": "Guided by the above clear, timeless vision and mission, the dedicated students, faculty and staff of AIT are set to steer the Institute along its path of becoming: A trailblazer in advanced education in the region, with leadership in IT and new types of multidisciplinary programs An exemplary institution, with an emphasis on academic quality in terms of courses and other aspects of operation A leader in professional development programs A hub for the implementation of regional and transnational research projects, and a research facility for academic professionals", "metadata": {"source": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "doc_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about", "chunk_index": 6, "chunk_len_chars": 569, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:23:14.120093+00:00"}}, {"rank": 5, "chunk_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about::c0000", "score": 0.2567598207569497, "text": "About - Asian Institute of Technology Home > About About AIT AIT is an international English-speaking postgraduate institution, focusing on engineering, environment, and management studies. In this section About AIT Facts and figures Rankings Leadership People Meet our faculty members Meet our staff members Location Welcome to AIT The Asian Institute of Technology (AIT), founded in 1959, is a not-for-profit international English-speaking postgraduate institution located on a green campus north of Bangkok, Thailand. AIT offers the opportunity to study at an institution in Asia which possesses a global reputation. Going forward, AIT will be stressing its global connections, injection of innovation into research and teaching, its relevance to industry, and its nurturing of entrepreneurship, while continuing to fulfill its social impact and capacity building role", "metadata": {"source": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about/", "doc_id": "https://www.ait.ac.th/about", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_len_chars": 871, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}], "model": "qwen3:8b"}

{"timestamp_utc": "2026-02-06T21:38:40.142448+00:00", "user_text": "Can I apply to two Academic Programs at the same time?", "assistant_text": "The Asian Institute of Technology (AIT) allows students to apply to multiple academic programs simultaneously, provided they meet the specific requirements and deadlines for each program. This flexibility is supported by the structure of AIT's admissions process, which does not restrict applicants from applying to more than one program at the same time.

However, it is important to note that each program may have its own set of eligibility criteria, application deadlines, and required documents. Therefore, while applying to two programs is permitted, applicants must ensure they are able to meet all the conditions for each program they choose to apply to. This includes submitting all necessary materials, adhering to deadlines, and fulfilling any additional requirements such as minimum academic performance or specific coursework. 

In summary, applying to two academic programs at AIT is allowed, but applicants must carefully manage their application process to ensure compliance with the requirements of each program.", "metrics": {"generation": {"model": "qwen3:8b", "created_at": "2026-02-06T21:38:40.094607874Z", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration_ns": 4680830085, "load_duration_ns": 82553884, "prompt_eval_count": 2882, "prompt_eval_duration_ns": 812867518, "eval_count": 177, "eval_duration_ns": 3720544887, "wall_time_s": 4.713414529920556, "requested_think": false, "observed_has_thinking_field": false, "tokens_per_second_out": 47.57367680698002}, "retrieval": {"retrieval_wall_time_s": 0.062013920978643, "top_k": 5, "n_returned": 5, "collection_name": "test_v1", "query_len_chars": 54, "has_scores": true, "retrieved_chunk_ids_ranked": ["https://ait.ac.th/academics/study-options::c0001", "https://ait.ac.th/apply-online::c0000", "https://ait.ac.th/program/university-of-nice-sophia-antipolis-france::c0001", "https://ait.ac.th/eligibility/doctoral-degree-program::c0001", "https://ait.ac.th/study/open-master-of-engineering-science-in-interdisciplinary-studies-omis::c0009"], "retrieved_source_urls_ranked": ["https://ait.ac.th/academics/study-options/", "https://ait.ac.th/apply-online/", "https://ait.ac.th/program/university-of-nice-sophia-antipolis-france", "https://ait.ac.th/eligibility/doctoral-degree-program/", "https://ait.ac.th/study/open-master-of-engineering-science-in-interdisciplinary-studies-omis"]}}, "retrieval_chunks": [{"rank": 1, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/academics/study-options::c0001", "score": 0.342794699309414, "text": "Tailor your studies to your interests and aspirations. In this section Academic calendar Academic Programs / Areas of Specialization Study options Student opportunities Faculties Master’s Degree Programs Doctoral Degree Programs Open Master of Engineering/Science in Interdisciplinary Studies (OMIS) Minor in Entrepreneurship Flexible Master’s Option Erasmus Programs Unified Degree Programs Joint Degree Programs Dual Degree Programs Professional Master’s Programs Certificate Programs Flexible PhD Option One Year Master’s Degree Program Academics Academic calendar Academic Programs / Areas of Specialization Study options Student opportunities Faculties Subscribe to our newsletter Subscribe to our newsletter Follow us on social media We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits. By clicking “Accept All”, you consent to the use of ALL the cookies", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/academics/study-options/", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/academics/study-options", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_len_chars": 929, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 2, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/apply-online::c0000", "score": 0.3702706407855011, "text": "Apply Now for Admissions to AIT | AIT Online Application Home > Apply online Apply online AIT welcomes talented, high-achieving students who contribute a wide diversity of views, experiences and perspectives. In this section Admissions Eligibility Financial aid Tuition and fees Student housing Apply online Frequently Asked Questions Start your application Complete your Online Application by clicking the ‘Apply Now’ button below. Apply now Deadlines and notifications for Application The AIT academic year consists of two semesters: January and August", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/apply-online/", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/apply-online", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_len_chars": 554, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 3, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/program/university-of-nice-sophia-antipolis-france::c0001", "score": 0.3715042556809338, "text": "The double degree is completed after doing an internship in a company or a research study in Europe. Students will be awarded two Master degrees: one from UNS and one from AIT. Apply Now Program brochure Subscribe to our newsletter Subscribe to our newsletter Follow us on social media We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits. By clicking “Accept All”, you consent to the use of ALL the cookies. However, you may visit "Cookie Settings" to provide a controlled consent. Cookie Settings Accept All Manage consent Close Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to improve your experience while you navigate through the website. Out of these, the cookies that are categorized as necessary are stored on your browser as they are essential for the working of basic functionalities of the website. We also use third-party cookies that help us analyze and understand how you use this website", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/program/university-of-nice-sophia-antipolis-france", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/program/university-of-nice-sophia-antipolis-france", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_len_chars": 967, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 4, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/eligibility/doctoral-degree-program::c0001", "score": 0.374456297719608, "text": "Two recommendation letters. * Applicants with a one-year master’s degree, a one-year professional master’s degree, or a one-year postgraduate diploma can enroll in the doctoral program by completing an additional 12-24 credits of coursework, obtaining a CGPA of 3.5, and achieving a very good or excellent grade in their research study, in addition to the required 84 credits for the doctoral program. Apply Here https://www.ait.ac.th/admissions/application-form/ Subscribe to our newsletter Subscribe to our newsletter Follow us on social media We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits. By clicking “Accept All”, you consent to the use of ALL the cookies. However, you may visit "Cookie Settings" to provide a controlled consent. Cookie Settings Accept All Manage consent Close Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to improve your experience while you navigate through the website", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/eligibility/doctoral-degree-program/", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/eligibility/doctoral-degree-program", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_len_chars": 967, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 5, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/open-master-of-engineering-science-in-interdisciplinary-studies-omis::c0009", "score": 0.3748292104325943, "text": "How to Apply? To apply, go to the AIT online application form by Clicking Here and choose “Open Master of Engineering/Science in Interdisciplinary Studies”. You also need to submit a Study Plan and a Research Plan in addition to the other required documents. Deadline The application deadline is like our other programs. Check Deadline Payment The payment follows the same process as for other programs. All details to make payments are at this website, Click here. Contact & Support For more Inquiry, please contact the us at this email: [email protected] Apply Now Program brochure For more information Click this link Subscribe to our newsletter Subscribe to our newsletter Follow us on social media We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits. By clicking “Accept All”, you consent to the use of ALL the cookies. However, you may visit "Cookie Settings" to provide a controlled consent", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/study/open-master-of-engineering-science-in-interdisciplinary-studies-omis", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/open-master-of-engineering-science-in-interdisciplinary-studies-omis", "chunk_index": 9, "chunk_len_chars": 966, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}], "model": "qwen3:8b"}

{"timestamp_utc": "2026-02-06T21:39:07.503994+00:00", "user_text": "How long does it take to complete a PhD program at AIT?", "assistant_text": "The typical duration of a PhD program at AIT is **6 years** when following the **Flexible Ph.D. Option**. This option allows students to complete their program at their own pace, with the flexibility to take courses online from home and only come to the AIT campus for specific activities such as labs, research work, and the graduation ceremony. 

While the Flexible Ph.D. Option provides a total flexible time of **6 years**, it is important to note that the program is not fully online. Students are still required to come to campus for certain academic activities. Additionally, the program has the same cost as the regular "On-Campus Option," and AIT offers scholarships for eligible candidates.

In summary, the **Flexible Ph.D. Option** typically takes **6 years** to complete, offering students the flexibility to balance their studies with other commitments.", "metrics": {"generation": {"model": "qwen3:8b", "created_at": "2026-02-06T21:39:07.463103814Z", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration_ns": 5218660257, "load_duration_ns": 79461044, "prompt_eval_count": 3968, "prompt_eval_duration_ns": 1242921478, "eval_count": 174, "eval_duration_ns": 3824772003, "wall_time_s": 5.250707352999598, "requested_think": false, "observed_has_thinking_field": false, "tokens_per_second_out": 45.49290777686128}, "retrieval": {"retrieval_wall_time_s": 2.0062091959407553, "top_k": 5, "n_returned": 5, "collection_name": "test_v1", "query_len_chars": 55, "has_scores": true, "retrieved_chunk_ids_ranked": ["https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-phd-option::c0001", "https://ait.ac.th/program/environmental-engineering-and-management::c0005", "https://ait.ac.th/study/one-year-masters-degree-program::c0002", "https://ait.ac.th/program/water-engineering-and-management-wem::c0006", "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-masters-option::c0001"], "retrieved_source_urls_ranked": ["https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-phd-option", "https://ait.ac.th/program/environmental-engineering-and-management", "https://ait.ac.th/study/one-year-masters-degree-program", "https://ait.ac.th/program/water-engineering-and-management-wem", "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-masters-option"]}}, "retrieval_chunks": [{"rank": 1, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-phd-option::c0001", "score": 0.21060106943858004, "text": "In coordination with the Program Chair, students may come to campus in short blocks or for entire semesters. This is not an online program; students still need to come to the AIT Campus for certain activities such as labs or research work and the graduation ceremony. However, we will allow high flexibility for such activities at our beautiful green AIT Campus in Thailand. The total flexible time to complete the program is 6 years. Advantages The Flexible Ph.D. Option gives you the flexibility you need! Flexible Time Management, “study when you’re free”, take courses online from home. Flexible Payment management, “pay as you study”, payment course-by-course. No need to come to the AIT Campus for most of your coursework. Work & Study at your own pace from any location. Cost The Flexible Ph.D. Option has the same cost as our regular “On-Campus Option”. However, all Schools provide AIT Scholarships for eligible candidates. To give you more flexibility, we allow you to pay course-by-course", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-phd-option", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-phd-option", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_len_chars": 999, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 2, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/program/environmental-engineering-and-management::c0005", "score": 0.21572392361725556, "text": "Doctoral Program The Doctoral program requires a minimum of 84 credits that comprise a minimum of 12 credits of coursework at AIT, which may include 3-credits of special study. This minimum credit requirement must be completed before the student is advanced to candidacy. The dissertation is worth 72 credits for the regular doctoral program. Concerned Faculty Members Prof.", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/program/environmental-engineering-and-management", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/program/environmental-engineering-and-management", "chunk_index": 5, "chunk_len_chars": 374, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 3, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/one-year-masters-degree-program::c0002", "score": 0.21737715472934882, "text": "OBTAIN SAME COUREWORK KNOWLEDGE AS THOSE TAKING REGULAR/TRADITIONAL MASTERS PROGRAMS: At AIT, students taking the accelerated option sit in the same classes at those taking two years programs. The only difference is that regular Master’s Programs include thesis, internship, exchange and ‘minors’ options (note: for those who might want to complete a PhD in the future, completion of a research thesis when completing a Master’s is a highly recommended path). AIT Programs that can be completed in two semesters (10 months) Please click on the link to find out more information about each program", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/study/one-year-masters-degree-program", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/one-year-masters-degree-program", "chunk_index": 2, "chunk_len_chars": 596, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 4, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/program/water-engineering-and-management-wem::c0006", "score": 0.2206506606037949, "text": "Doctoral Program The Doctoral program requires a minimum of 84 credits that comprise a minimum of 12 credits of coursework at AIT, which may include 3-credits of special study. This minimum credit requirement must be completed before the student is advanced to candidacy. The dissertation is worth 72 credits for the regular doctoral program. Concerned Faculty Prof. Sangam Shrestha Professor, Director Dr.", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/program/water-engineering-and-management-wem", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/program/water-engineering-and-management-wem", "chunk_index": 6, "chunk_len_chars": 406, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}, {"rank": 5, "chunk_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-masters-option::c0001", "score": 0.23965044504694, "text": "All classes are recorded for later viewing. After completion of the coursework, students can do their research or thesis in the AIT Campus at a flexible time. In coordination with the Program Chair, students may come to campus in short blocks or up to 11 months, typically for thesis research work. This is not an online program; students still need to come to the AIT Campus for certain activities such as labs or research work and the graduation ceremony. However, we will allow high flexibility for such activities at our beautiful green AIT Campus in Thailand. Total flexible time to complete the program is 2 years at full time and 4 years as part time. Advantages The Flexible Master’s Option gives you the flexibility you need! Flexible Time Management, “study when you’re free” , take courses online from home. Flexible Payment management, “pay as you study” , payment course-by-course. No need to come to the AIT Campus for most of your coursework", "metadata": {"source": "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-masters-option", "doc_id": "https://ait.ac.th/study/flexible-masters-option", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_len_chars": 956, "ingested_at_utc": "2026-01-27T07:28:48.804207+00:00"}}], "model": "qwen3:8b"}
